### Throws & Throws
Key Points to Remember

. throw is used to actually send an exception when something goes wrong during execution.
. throws is used to declare that a method might throw an exception - it warns the caller.
. throw goes inside the method body; throws goes in the method declaration.
. You can only throw one exception at a time, but you can throws multiple exceptions.
. throw happens during runtime, while throws is checked at compile-time.
. Both are used for exception handling, but they play very different roles.
